  "CALL_LINES": [
    "The ten-year is trading at 4.74 percent this morning, about 24 basis points above our 4.50 percent underwriting base, as Fed Governor Waller opens the door to holding rates steady this month.",
    "Oil is holding just above 91 dollars a barrel on the Iran standoff, and every basis point that premium keeps in the ten-year raises our cost of capital into the September 16 FOMC decision.",
    "The S&P is near 7,700, up about four tenths of a percent, but the ten-year sets our cost of capital, and today's pullback in yields is the number that matters for locks."
